Function.Description:
Inserts the given agent in the process flow by outputting it from the out port.
Depending on the value of {@link #pushProtocol}, agent may leave this block at the same time or later.
@see #cancel(Agent)

Returns the iterator over agents currently pending transmission in this block (which has't yet been consumed by subsequent flowchart blocks) - in their <code>take()</code> order.<br>
Note that returned agents may be consumed by subsecuent block at any time later (e.g. some Delay gets free, or Hold unblocks) - unless {@link cancel(Agent)} funtion is called.
Usage:
for (Agent agent : block) {
}

