Function.Description:
Removes the agent stored in a given cell [row,position,level] from the rack system and returns it.
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@param leftAisle [for 2-aisle pallet racks]: from which aisle the agent should be removed: from the left or from the right one
@return the removed agent

Returns the agent stored at the specified cell [row,position,level,deepPosition], or <code>null</code> if the cell is reserved or free.
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@param deepPosition [if cells have depth] the index (0, 1, ..), counted from the aisle (or from the left aisle, if there are several aisles near this row)
@return the agent stored at the specified cell

Puts the agent into the cell with the specified coordinates [row,position,level]. If the cell is occupied, signals error. Does not check if the cell is reserved.
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@param leftAisle [for 2-aisle pallet racks]: from which aisle the agent should be put to the cell: from the left or from the right one
@param agent the agent

Tests if a given cell [row,position,level] is reserved and returns the number of reserved slots in the depth of the cell.
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@return the number of reserved locations (may be > 1 for pallet racks with depth)

Returns the coordinates of a cell with a given agent [row,position,level], or null if the agent is not stored here.
@param agent the agent
@return [row,position,level], or <code>null</code>

Marks a given cell [row,position,level] as reserved. The cell must be free.
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@param leftAisle [for 2-aisle pallet racks]: from which aisle the cell reserve should be placed

Discards a reservation of a given cell [row,position,level]. The cell must be reserved.
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@param leftAisle [for 2-aisle pallet racks]: from which aisle the cell reserve should be released

Returns the array [row,position,level] with the coordinates of a free cell  that is closest to either front of back of the rack system, depending on the parameter infront. If the rack system is full, returns null.
@param infront if <code>true</code>, the returned object will have the smallest available {@linkplain PalletRackLocation#position position}
@return the [row,position,level]

Removes a given agent from the rack system and returns it. If the agent is not stored here, returns null.
@param agent the agent to remove
@return the agent if was removed, otherwise <code>null</code>

Returns the position at the given cell
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@param deepPosition [if cells have depth] the index (0, 1, ..), counted from the aisle (or from the left aisle, if there are several aisles near this row)
@param offset offset within cell
@param depth depth within cell
@param leftAisle [for 2-aisle pallet racks, needed for orientation calculation]: where the face of agent should be oriented: as it was put from the left aisle or from the right one
@param out any {@link Position} object (to be used for output) or <code>null</code> (in this case, new Position object will be created)
@return the position at the given cell

Returns the stored agent with a given index. The order of agents is internal and may change when agents are added or removed. If the index is greater than the number of agents-1, returns <code>null</code>.
@param index the index
@return agent by index or <code>null</code>

Tests if a given cell [row,position,level] is free, i.e. neither occupied nor reserved.
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@return <code>true</code> if free

Returns the position in the pallet rack aisle located in front of a cell with a given row and position (level does not matter as cells located one above the other have aisle position).
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param leftAisle [for 2-aisle pallet racks, needed for orientation calculation]: where the face of agent should be oriented: as it was put from the left aisle or from the right one
@param out any {@link Position} object (to be used for output) or <code>null</code> (in this case, new Position object will be created)
@return the position in the pallet rack aisle located in front of a cell

Removes the agent stored in a given cell [row,position,level] from the rack system and returns it.
@param location the [row,position,level]
@param leftAisle [for 2-aisle pallet racks]: from which aisle the agent should be removed: from the left or from the right one
@return the removed agent

Tests if a given cell [row,position,level] is free, i.e. neither occupied nor reserved and returns the number of free slots in the depth of the cell
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@return the number of free slots in the depth of the cell

Returns the position at the enter to the given cell
@param row the row (0, 1, ..)
@param position the position in row (0, 1, ..)
@param level the level (0 is the lowest)
@param leftAisle [for 2-aisle pallet racks, needed for orientation calculation]: where the face of agent should be oriented: as it was put from the left aisle or from the right one
@param out any {@link Position} object (to be used for output) or <code>null</code> (in this case, new Position object will be created)
@return the position at the enter to the given cell

Return the approach direction to the given agent or <code>null</code> if agent is unreachable (lies deep in the cell, behind other agents)
@param agent the agent
@param rowToSearch optional parameter - the row previously found by {@link #getCellOf(Agent)} (set to -1 if unknown)
@return the approach direction

